Project-authored mobile-use source is licensed under the root MIT license.
Third-party dependencies retain their own licenses; the MIT project license
does not replace them. In particular, the bundled Model Context Protocol
server/core packages retain their Apache-2.0 and applicable MIT notices.

The plugin build appends license/notice texts for dependencies actually included
in its server bundle. When a published npm package omits its license file, a
version-specific upstream license and immutable source provenance are retained
in the source repository under third_party/npm-licenses. The build fails if
neither license source is available.

The MCP SDK also embeds dependencies that are not visible as separate esbuild
inputs. Its version-pinned embedded-dependency audit is retained in the source
repository under third_party/npm-licenses. The build includes their complete
license texts below, without duplicating the source audit records in the plugin.
An SDK update requires a new audit; missing audit/license/provenance files fail
the build rather than silently omitting embedded dependency notices.

Android Platform-Tools, Node.js, OEM drivers, and phone-side software are not
redistributed by this plugin.
